Notes:
	A hand-written WalkForward: section -- the in-sample / out-of-sample split
	form that needs no optimization.  N dates define N-1 intervals, so each
	parameter row carries N-1 values.  (An optimizer-generated section has the
	same shape, with one date per interval.)
	A Namespace: prefix and a WalkForward: parameter list do not mix: RealTest
	namespaces the row names too, and then cannot match them to the parameters.

Settings:
	DataFile:	feature_tests.rtd
	AccountSize:	100000

Parameters:
	nLen:	20
	nMult:	from 1 to 3 step 0.5 def 2 {x}

Strategy: wf
	EntrySetup:	C > MA(C, nLen)
	ExitStop:	FillPrice - nMult * ATR(nLen)
	MaxPositions:	nLen

WalkForward:
	Dates:	1/1/2000, 1/1/2010, 1/1/2018
	nLen:	10, 20
	nMult:	1.5, 2
